<BaseLayout title="SIP calculator" description="Estimate SIP value with transparent monthly assumptions."><section class="wrap py-12"><h1 class="mb-6 text-4xl font-bold">SIP calculator</h1><SipCalculator /><article class="prose max-w-3xl"><h2>How this estimate works</h2><p>A Systematic Investment Plan invests a chosen amount regularly into a mutual fund. This tool assumes each contribution happens at the end of a month, with a nominal annual rate divided by 12 and compounded monthly. For example, ₹5,000 monthly for 10 years at an assumed 10% produces an illustration—not a promise.</p><h2>What it does not model</h2><p>Actual NAV movement, taxes, fund expenses, missed instalments and changing returns are not included. Compare assumptions carefully and read <a href="/blog/what-is-a-sip/">our SIP explainer</a>.</p></article></section></BaseLayout>
